id: pm-q7c36n
title: Registry install acceptance loses subprocess timeout and signal evidence and labels every failure as registry availability
description: "The 2026-09-28 Windows npm-global acceptance job failed after three approximately 120-second install attempts. Its only terminal diagnosis was installer exited non-zero. Source inspection shows runCommand normalizes a null status to 1 and discards spawn error and signal, while installAndRun labels every retry registry availability. The later exact-version recovery passed, which proves recoverability but not the cause of the original failure. Preserve classified bounded evidence so reliability improvements target measured causes."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:release",diagnostics,"horizon:current",recurrence-prevention
created_at: "2026-09-28T05:47:28.714Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-29T10:50:28.772Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-29T10:50:28.123Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-29T10:50:28.123Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Positive and negative tests distinguish timeout, signal termination, ENOENT, nonzero exit, transient registry visibility and successful install without falsely attributing unknown causes to the registry; Keep install attempt and total-job deadlines bounded and preserve original failed attempt receipts after recovery; Local and hosted npm local/global and bun acceptance use the same classification with privacy-safe bounded stderr"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Retain raw subprocess outcomes; classify only complete, redacted registry output before excerpt truncation; redact complete Authorization values; match origin-bearing exact-tag recovery runs."
expected_result: "npm/Bun acceptance distinguishes failure causes, retries explicit registry 404 even after long output, and never exposes authorization values in retained receipts."
actual_result: "42 linked installer tests and 9 selector tests passed; full suite 9,430 passed with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; PR #1350 reviewer defects corrected pending hosted re-review."
