comments[3]:
  - created_at: "2026-09-28T05:47:28.714Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Duplicate check 2026-09-28: complete 2826-item all-status metadata/history corpus and keyword AND searches for registry installer timeout diagnostics, installation retries, and subprocess error installer. Existing published-metadata propagation owner pm-wzmbvn concerns npm view visibility, not lost install subprocess diagnostics. Existing global reinstall owner pm-ir9vqy concerns missing executable, not acceptance failure classification. Sources: scripts/release/utils.mjs runCommand and scripts/release/verify-installed-agent-session.mjs installAndRun; https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/36377133727 and recovery https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/36380136948."
    edited_at: "2026-09-28T07:20:10.255Z"
  - created_at: "2026-09-29T10:00:26.151Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Implemented classified installer receipts for timeout, signal, ENOENT, other spawn error, nonzero exit, and registry 404. Registry visibility alone retries up to three attempts; every failed attempt remains in the success or failure evidence. Stderr excerpts are bounded to 512 characters with credential redaction. One 13-minute deadline covers control and candidate sessions under the hosted 15-minute job. Verification: linked unit tests passed (41); full coverage suite passed 9,428 tests at 100/100/100/100; packed package initialized, created, and read back items under both npm and Bun in separate temporary roots. Hosted matrix evidence awaits this PR and is not claimed as run locally."
  - created_at: "2026-09-29T10:28:53.508Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "PR #1350 review found 404 detection ran after stderr truncation and Authorization: token value redaction was incomplete. Classification now reads the full redacted diagnostic before the excerpt is bounded; test covers a 404 beyond 512 characters and a complete authorization value. Greptile discussions #4132270490 and #4132270496."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T10:00:26.761Z","harness:codex","Recovery must preserve the original installer process cause. A public-registry 404 can represent propagation delay; timeout, signal, spawn failure, and generic nonzero exits provide no such evidence and therefore fail without another registry retry."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T10:00:27.539Z","harness:codex","Keep raw spawn status separate from the normalized command status: a null exit status plus ETIMEDOUT or a signal is materially different from exit code 1. Bound and redact process diagnostics before retaining them in acceptance receipts."
